.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt LIBPOWERCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm powercmp_client_open ,
.Nm powercmp_client_close ,
.Nm powercmp_states ,
.Nm powercmp_suspend
.Nd client for the system.Power capability
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libpowercmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In powercmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_client_open "struct powercmp_client **clientp"
.Ft void
.Fn powercmp_client_close "struct powercmp_client *client"
\.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_states "struct powercmp_client *client" "uint32_t *supported"
.Ft int
.Fn powercmp_suspend "struct powercmp_client *client" "uint32_t state"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libpowercmp
 is the client to
.Xr BSDPower 8 ,
the
.Dq system.Power
capability provider.
.Fn powercmp_states
returns the supported ACPI sleep states as a bitmask (bit N set means SN);
reads are unprivileged.
.Fn powercmp_suspend
requests the machine enter sleep state
.Fa state
(1\(en5), which needs privilege the sandboxed caller lacks; the broker performs
it after a per-label policy check.
.Pp
.Fn powercmp_client_open
opens a session and returns 0, or -1 with
.Va errno
set.
.Fn powercmp_suspend
fails with
.Er EPERM
when the caller's label is not granted suspend authority.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr BSDPower 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
